WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.500
After years of buildup, Batman finally got
the band together in Justice League to save

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.250
the world from certain doom.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.049
But there are still a ton of questions about
how exactly they managed to do it.

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:15.730
So hold on to your Mother Box, because here's
a spoiler-filled look at some of the biggest

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.680
unanswered questions in Justice League.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.530
What happened to the Mother Box?

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.360
The plot of Justice League revolves around
the villainous Steppenwolf assembling the

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.750
Mother Box and almost wiping out the whole
world.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:32.750
Luckily, Cyborg and Superman team up to pull
the box apart in the nick of time, and everyone

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.260
goes away happy.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.699
But what happened to the Mother Box after
that?

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:40.710
Considering it has the power to bend time
and space and destroy entire planets, you'd

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.960
think the Justice League would want to keep
a really close eye on it.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.540
But for some reason the box is never seen
again.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.460
And where it ended up is just one big question
we have about the Mother Box, the other one

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.460
being…

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:53.460
"what's in the box?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.300
What's in the the f------ box?!"

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.040
What about Darkseid?

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:03.100
In Batman versus Superman, we got a whole
dream sequence teasing the arrival of the

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.150
ultimate big bad in the DC Extended Universe,
Darkseid.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.330
So it was pretty weird that he was barely
even mentioned in Justice League, especially

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.440
considering almost the entire movie is about
him.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.820
See, Steppenwolf works for Darkseid, and the
Mother Box is trying to turn Earth into a

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.210
new version of the planet Apokolips.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.760
Which is also where the parademons come from.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.690
And presumably where the boom tube teleportation
tornados lead to.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.910
So this movie was really all about Darkseid.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:34.380
But when it comes to the DCEU, who is he?

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.510
What does he want?

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.520
And when is he going to show up on screen?

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.440
Those are all questions Justice League asks,
but doesn't answer.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.280
What's the deal with Cyborg?

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.330
In Batman versus Superman and Justice League,
we learn that Cyborg's cyborgian bits were

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:54.270
created by the Mother Box, which basically
overwrote his damaged body with Apokoliptian

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.270
technology.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:02:00.150
Both Aquaman and Cyborg himself raise concerns
that the Mother Box may turn Cyborg against

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:04.790
the Justice League, but other than one stray
missile fired at Superman's face, nothing

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:05.820
comes of it.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.800
Well...nothing comes of it yet.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.030
But what happens when Cyborg faces Darkseid,
the master of Apokolips?

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.480
Does the Justice League have an unwitting
mole inside their group, a double agent infected

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.049
with an alien virus that's waiting to betray
Earth at just the wrong time?

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:25.290
Maybe before Batman builds his special table
in Justice League Mansion, he should consider

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.599
exactly what kind of ticking time bomb he's
letting on the team.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:31.340
Where was Green Lantern?

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:35.610
In maybe the movie's coolest moment, fans
finally got the see the Green Lantern Corps

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:40.379
brought into the DC Extended Universe in a
flashback sequence, where they team up with

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:46.310
the Amazons, Atlanteans, Old Gods, and regular
schmoes to take down Steppenwolf when he first

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.079
attacked Earth thousands of years ago.

00:02:49.079 --> 00:02:52.840
One question, though: where the heck was Green
Lantern during the fight at the end of the

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.840
movie?

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.739
Green Lanterns are basically the beat cops
of the universe, and since Darkseid and the

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:02.489
forces of Apokolips are pretty much the single
biggest threat in that universe, you'd think

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:06.209
an APB would be put out as soon as that Mother
Box starts shimmying.

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:10.139
And yet there's no sign of any Green Lanterns
in the present day at all.

00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:12.019
Was he at a cosmic donut shop?

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.600
Hopefully the next time the world is about
to be destroyed, he'll bother to show up.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.700
"Stand back and peep the light show! Green Lantern's got this!"

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.960
Green 
Lantern wasn't the only no show though...

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:30.829
Where was everyone else?

00:03:30.829 --> 00:03:35.859
When Steppenwolf attacked thousands of years
ago, a massive alliance came together to stop

00:03:35.859 --> 00:03:36.859
him.

00:03:36.859 --> 00:03:40.980
This time around, though, a handful of weirdos
in costumes are the only people who bother

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.139
to lift a finger.

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:44.430
So where was everyone else?

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.469
For no apparent reason, the Amazons suddenly
aren't allowed to leave their island.

00:03:48.469 --> 00:03:51.290
But why weren't the Atlanteans there to help
the Justice League?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.739
How about, you know, the Russian Army, who
had to be wondering about what was going on

00:03:55.739 --> 00:03:57.239
at that reactor site?

00:03:57.239 --> 00:04:00.970
And what about other characters in the DC
Extended Universe, like the Suicide Squad?

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:01.970
Remember them?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.760
"I want to assemble a task force of the most
dangerous people on the planet."

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.969
It seems really weird that nobody else on
the planet cared whether or not Earth was

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:11.209
destroyed.

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:13.709
How do they explain Clark's return?

00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:17.709
Most of Justice League revolves around how
much the world needs Superman, and the team's

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:20.299
successful efforts to bring him back to life.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:25.030
But how is anyone going to be able to spin
Clark Kent's revival without giving away the

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.120
obvious fact that he's Superman? Clark got
an obituary and a funeral in Batman versus

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.680
Superman, but now he's back in his old house,
and walking the streets of Metropolis like

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.370
nothing ever happened.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:40.759
Between that and Lois referring to Superman
as "Clark" right out in the open, it seems

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:46.120
like they may have brought back Superman only
to kill his secret identity in the process.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.009
Who is in the Legion of Doom?

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:53.699
Finally, we just have to ask: who else is
going to be in Lex Luthor's Legion of Doom?

00:04:53.699 --> 00:04:57.680
So far in the end credits scene, we have Lex
and Deathstroke the Terminator, but if the

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:03.169
Super Friends cartoon is any indication, we
can expect to see more villains in the future.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:08.270
The Joker, of course, has already shown up
in Suicide Squad, but other bad guys like

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:13.730
Black Manta, Captain Cold, and the Cheetah
have yet to make their debuts in the DC Extended

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.730
Universe.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.669
Frankly, we don't care who is on the team
— as long as Lex trades in that yacht for

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:23.300
a headquarters that looks like Darth Vader's
helmet and rests at the bottom of a swamp.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.560
Give the fans what they want!

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.560
Thanks for watching!

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.360
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.900
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

